## Scenarios

### MIR method-call strict shared bindings

#### lowers Result.unwrap to a discriminant-guarded payload extraction with an Err panic path

- Verify: lowers Result.unwrap to a discriminant-guarded payload extraction with an Err panic path
   - Expected: mir.functions.keys().len() equals `1`
   - Expected: labels contains `result_unwrap_payload`
   - Expected: labels contains `result_unwrap_mismatch`
   - Expected: labels contains `result_unwrap_merge`
   - Expected: calls contains `rt_enum_discriminant`
   - Expected: calls contains `rt_enum_payload`
   - Expected: calls contains `rt_panic`
   - Expected: mir_const_strings(fn_) contains `called `.unwrap()` on an Err Result`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 18 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-COMPILER-BOOTSTRAP-001
step("Verify: lowers Result.unwrap to a discriminant-guarded payload extraction with an Err panic path")
val source = "fn take(r: Result<i64, text>) -> i64:\n    return r.unwrap()\n"
val mir = lower_fixture(source, "result_unwrap_mod")
expect(mir.functions.keys().len()).to_equal(1)
val fn_ = mir.functions.values()[0]
var labels: [text] = []
for block in fn_.blocks:
    if val label = block.label:
        labels.push(label)
expect(labels.contains("result_unwrap_payload")).to_equal(true)
expect(labels.contains("result_unwrap_mismatch")).to_equal(true)
expect(labels.contains("result_unwrap_merge")).to_equal(true)
val calls = mir_call_targets(fn_)
expect(calls.contains("rt_enum_discriminant")).to_equal(true)
expect(calls.contains("rt_enum_payload")).to_equal(true)
expect(calls.contains("rt_panic")).to_equal(true)
expect(mir_const_strings(fn_).contains("called `.unwrap()` on an Err Result")).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

#### derives the Err payload type for unwrap_err and panics on Ok

- Verify: derives the Err payload type for unwrap_err and panics on Ok
   - Expected: mir_call_targets(fn_) contains `rt_panic`
   - Expected: mir_const_strings(fn_) contains `called `.unwrap_err()` on an Ok Result`
   - Expected: mir_call_targets(fn_) contains `rt_interp_cstr`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 10 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-COMPILER-BOOTSTRAP-001
step("Verify: derives the Err payload type for unwrap_err and panics on Ok")
val source = "fn take_err(r: Result<i64, text>) -> text:\n    return r.unwrap_err()\n"
val mir = lower_fixture(source, "result_unwrap_err_mod")
val fn_ = mir.functions.values()[0]
expect(mir_call_targets(fn_).contains("rt_panic")).to_equal(true)
expect(mir_const_strings(fn_).contains("called `.unwrap_err()` on an Ok Result")).to_equal(true)
# Err payloads travel as text: the mismatch arm renders through the
# interpreter c-string decoder, not the raw i64 renderer.
expect(mir_call_targets(fn_).contains("rt_interp_cstr")).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

#### routes unwrap_or through the default-value arm instead of the panic path

- Verify: routes unwrap_or through the default-value arm instead of the panic path
   - Expected: mir_call_targets(fn_) does not contain `rt_panic`
   - Expected: mir_const_strings(fn_) does not contain `called `.unwrap()` on an Err Result`
   - Expected: mir_call_targets(fn_) contains `rt_enum_payload`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 8 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-COMPILER-BOOTSTRAP-001
step("Verify: routes unwrap_or through the default-value arm instead of the panic path")
val source = "fn or_default(r: Result<i64, text>) -> i64:\n    return r.unwrap_or(9)\n"
val mir = lower_fixture(source, "result_unwrap_or_mod")
val fn_ = mir.functions.values()[0]
expect(mir_call_targets(fn_).contains("rt_panic")).to_equal(false)
expect(mir_const_strings(fn_).contains("called `.unwrap()` on an Err Result")).to_equal(false)
expect(mir_call_targets(fn_).contains("rt_enum_payload")).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

#### resolves struct method calls through the struct-method symbol table

- Verify: resolves struct method calls through the struct-method symbol table
   - Expected: mir.functions.keys().len() >= 2 is true
   - Expected: names contains `go`
   - Expected: call_count >= 1 is true


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 25 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-COMPILER-BOOTSTRAP-001
step("Verify: resolves struct method calls through the struct-method symbol table")
val source = "struct Box:\n    v: i64\n    me get() -> i64:\n        return self.v\n\nfn go() -> i64:\n    val b = Box(v: 4)\n    return b.get()\n"
val mir = lower_fixture(source, "struct_method_mod")
# Both the struct method and the caller lower to real MIR functions.
expect(mir.functions.keys().len() >= 2).to_equal(true)
var names: [text] = []
for key in mir.functions.keys():
    names.push(mir.functions[key].name)
expect(names.contains("go")).to_equal(true)
# The caller must contain an actual call instruction resolving to the
# struct method (not a decode/abort stub) plus a load of field v.
var go_fn = mir.functions[mir.functions.keys()[0]]
for key in mir.functions.keys():
    if mir.functions[key].name == "go":
        go_fn = mir.functions[key]
var call_count = 0
for block in go_fn.blocks:
    for inst in block.instructions:
        match inst.kind:
            case MirInstKind.Call(_, _, _):
                call_count += 1
            case _:
                ()
expect(call_count >= 1).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

